<%# Fuime: the parent-first teen's one email. See Fuime::FamilyMailer.

    Every claim here is true under merchant-of-record today: the parent's
    signature is done and it gates PAYOUTS; selling waits on Fuime's own human
    review, which is said plainly rather than implied away. No L5 vocabulary,
    no amount, no ETA. %>
<p>
  Hi <%= @greeting_name.presence || "there" %> —
</p>

<p>
  <strong><%= @guardian_name %></strong> signed as your parent or guardian on
  Fuime, a financial platform for young founders. That means you can set up a
  business and, once a person at Fuime approves it, sell what you make or do.
  <%= @guardian_first_name %> approves the money when you ask to be paid, and
  signing off was the part that had to happen first — that's already done.
</p>

<% if @existing_account %>
  <p>
    You already have a Fuime account — this just adds
    <%= @guardian_first_name %> to it as your parent or guardian.
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p>
    Your part: your name, one checkbox, and what your business does. About
    three minutes.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  <%= link_to (@existing_account ? "Open Fuime" : "Set up my business"), @join_url,
              style: "display:inline-block;background:#2242FF;color:#ffffff;padding:12px 20px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:8px;font-weight:600;" %>
</p>

<p style="word-break: break-all;">
  Or paste this link into your browser:<br>
  <%= @join_url %>
</p>

<p>
  The link works for <%= ::Fuime::FamilyInviteService::JOIN_EXPIRES_IN.inspect %>
  and signs you in on this browser with the same email this message was sent
  to. After that, go to <%= link_to auth_users_url, auth_users_url %> and we'll
  email you a login code.
</p>

<p>
  Not expecting this? Ignore it — nothing happens unless you open it.
</p>

<p>
  — the Fuime team
</p>
